IMPORT prelude

-- Workplace Safety and Health Act 2006 (Singapore) -- who is the occupier of a workplace (s 4(1) "occupier"), what a workplace
-- is (s 5(1)), the occupier's duty for the workplace and its means of access and egress to everyone within (s 11), the
-- employer's duties to its own employees at work and to others (s 12(1), (2)), the principal's duties to a contractor's
-- employees (ss 14(1)-(3), 14A(1)), the common-area occupier (s 19), duties held in several capacities at once and not
-- diminished by each other (s 10), who may be served with a remedial or stop-work order (s 21(2)), and the relation to other
-- written law (s 59).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/WSHA2006.txt ("version in
-- force from 1/12/2025"). Section numbers are taken from the body of the deposit; the arrangement table at its head runs one
-- line out of step from s 14 onward (it puts "Duties of persons at work" against 14A, which in the body is s 15).
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0288 (Haziq scenario, event h080): a security officer employed by an agency falls on a
-- wet stairwell in an office tower leased by a software company; what does the Act require of the company as occupier,
-- separately from what it requires of the agency as employer?
--
-- NOT ENCODED: what "so far as is reasonably practicable" requires on any facts (a standard, not a test; s 47 puts the onus on
-- the accused and is in wsha-duties.l4); occupiers of factories beyond the s 4(1) certificate-holder rule; the s 12(4) and
-- s 14(5) duties to give prescribed information (regulations not retrieved); s 12A platform operators and s 13 self-employed
-- persons; s 15 duties of the person at work himself; the accident-reporting duty under s 27 (regulations not retrieved); the
-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 (not deposited here) -- this Act mentions it only in s 27B(1), on the inadmissibility of
-- learning reports. Penalties are in wsha-duties.l4 (s 20 with s 50).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workplace Safety and Health Act 2006 -- occupier, employer and principal`

§§ `5(1), 19(1) -- the workplace and the place of the accident`

-- s 5(1): "'workplace' means any premises where a person is at work or is to work, for the time being works, or customarily
-- works, and includes a factory." s 4(1): "'premises' includes any place whether enclosed or built on or not ... (c) a part
-- of any premises".
-- s 19(1): "where a building comprises one or more workplaces, any common property or limited common property of the building
-- (called in this section the common area) which is used by persons at work in any such workplace or is used by such persons
-- to move through is treated as part of their workplace."
DECLARE Premises HAS
    `a person is at work there or customarily works there` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a factory requiring registration or notification` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Spot HAS
    `is within the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a means of access to or egress from the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is common property of a building comprising workplaces` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is used by persons at work there or to move through` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises are a workplace` IF
    `the premises`'s `a person is at work there or customarily works there`

GIVEN `the spot` IS A Spot
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the spot is a common area treated as part of the workplace` IF
        `the spot`'s `is common property of a building comprising workplaces`
    AND `the spot`'s `is used by persons at work there or to move through`

-- s 11 reaches "(a) the workplace; (b) all means of access to or egress from the workplace; and (c) any machinery, equipment,
-- plant, article or substance kept on the workplace". A common area under s 19(1) is part of the workplace.
GIVEN `the spot` IS A Spot
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the spot is within the reach of section 11` IF
        `the spot`'s `is within the workplace`
    OR  `the spot`'s `is a means of access to or egress from the workplace`
    OR  `the spot is a common area treated as part of the workplace` `the spot`

§§ `4(1) "occupier", 11 -- the occupier's duty`

-- s 4(1): "'occupier', in relation to any premises or part of any premises, means -- (a) [and (b)] in the case of a factory
-- where a certificate of registration has to be obtained [or a notification submitted] ... -- the person who is, or is
-- required to be, the holder of the certificate [or is named in, or required to submit, the notification]; and (c) in the case
-- of any other premises -- the person who has charge, management or control of those premises either on the person's own
-- account or as an agent of another person, whether or not the person is also the owner of those premises".
-- Ownership and leasehold are not the test: control is. (Whether a lessee has charge, management or control of a stairwell is a
-- question of fact, taken here as a flag.)
DECLARE DutyHolder HAS
    `has charge, management or control of the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds or must hold the factory certificate or notification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the owner of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employs the injured person under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employs anyone under a contract of service in its business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `engaged the injured person's employer to supply labour or do work for gain in its business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `directs the manner in which the injured person works` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carries on an undertaking in the workplace that may affect the injured person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date the contractor was engaged as yyyymmdd` IS A NUMBER
    `is the management corporation controlling the common area` IS A BOOLEAN
    `poses a risk to persons at work in the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Entrant HAS
    `is within the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is at work` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder, `the premises` IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the occupier of the workplace` IF
        (    `the premises`'s `is a factory requiring registration or notification`
         AND `the holder`'s `holds or must hold the factory certificate or notification`)
    OR  (    (NOT `the premises`'s `is a factory requiring registration or notification`)
         AND `the holder`'s `has charge, management or control of the workplace`)

-- s 11: "It is the duty of every occupier of any workplace to take, so far as is reasonably practicable, such measures to ensure
-- that -- (a) the workplace; (b) all means of access to or egress from the workplace; and (c) any machinery, equipment, plant,
-- article or substance kept on the workplace, are safe and without risks to health to every person within those premises,
-- whether or not the person is at work or is an employee of the occupier."
-- Whether the injured person is at work, or is anyone's employee, does not enter the test.
GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder, `the premises` IS A Premises, `the spot` IS A Spot, `the person` IS AN Entrant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owes the section 11 occupier's duty to the person for the spot` IF
        `is the occupier of the workplace` `the holder` `the premises`
    AND `the premises are a workplace` `the premises`
    AND `the spot is within the reach of section 11` `the spot`
    AND `the person`'s `is within the premises`

§§ `19(2), (3) -- the occupier of a common area`

-- s 19(2): "It is the duty of the occupier of the common area to comply with any provision of this Act with respect to -- ...
-- (c) means of access into or egress from the common area". s 19(3): "'occupier', in relation to a common area, includes the
-- management corporation or subsidiary management corporation (as the case may be) having control of that common area."
-- s 19(2) lists four subjects only: (a) electric generators and motors, (b) hoists and lifts, (c) means of access and egress,
-- (d) machinery or plant belonging to or supplied by the owner or occupier.
GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder, `the spot` IS A Spot
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owes the section 19 common-area duty for access and egress` IF
        `the spot is a common area treated as part of the workplace` `the spot`
    AND (    `the holder`'s `is the management corporation controlling the common area`
         OR  `the holder`'s `has charge, management or control of the workplace`)

§§ `6(1), 12 -- the employer's duties`

-- s 6(1): "'employer' means a person who, in the course of the person's trade, business, profession or undertaking, employs any
-- person to do any work under a contract of service."
-- s 4(1): "'at work' means -- (a) in relation to an employee, all times when the employee is performing work in connection with
-- any trade, business, profession or undertaking carried on by his or her employer, wherever that work is carried out".
-- s 12(1): "It is the duty of every employer to take, so far as is reasonably practicable, such measures as are necessary to
-- ensure the safety and health of the employer's employees at work." s 12(3)(a): those measures include "providing and
-- maintaining for those persons a work environment which is safe, without risk to health" and (c) ensuring they are not
-- exposed to hazards arising from things "(i) in their workplace; or (ii) near their workplace and under the control of the
-- employer"; (d) emergency procedures; (e) "adequate instruction, information, training and supervision".
-- The employer's duty follows the employee "wherever that work is carried out" -- including onto premises the employer does
-- not occupy.
GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an employer` IF
        `the holder`'s `employs anyone under a contract of service in its business`
    OR  `the holder`'s `employs the injured person under a contract of service`

GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder, `the person` IS AN Entrant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owes the section 12(1) duty to the person as its employee` IF
        `the holder`'s `employs the injured person under a contract of service`
    AND `the person`'s `is at work`

-- s 12(2): "It is the duty of every employer to take, so far as is reasonably practicable, such measures as are necessary to
-- ensure the safety and health of persons (not being the employer's employees) who may be affected by any undertaking carried
-- on by the employer in the workplace."
GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owes the section 12(2) duty to the person as a non-employee` IF
        `is an employer` `the holder`
    AND (NOT `the holder`'s `employs the injured person under a contract of service`)
    AND `the holder`'s `carries on an undertaking in the workplace that may affect the injured person`

§§ `4(1) "principal", 14, 14A -- the principal's duties`

-- s 4(1): "'principal' means a person who, in connection with any trade, business, profession or undertaking carried on by the
-- person, engages any other person otherwise than under a contract of service -- (a) to supply any labour for gain or reward;
-- or (b) to do any work for gain or reward". A firm that hires a security agency is, on that text, the agency's principal
-- (INFERENCE: that guarding the firm's offices is "in connection with" its business).
-- s 14(1): the principal must take reasonably practicable measures for the safety and health of "(c) any employee employed by
-- such contractor ... when at work". s 14(2): "The duty ... only applies where the contractor, subcontractor or employee ... is
-- working under the direction of the principal as to the manner in which the work is carried out."
GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the principal of the injured person's employer` IF
    `the holder`'s `engaged the injured person's employer to supply labour or do work for gain in its business`

GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder, `the person` IS AN Entrant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owes the section 14(1) duty to the contractor's employee` IF
        `is the principal of the injured person's employer` `the holder`
    AND `the person`'s `is at work`
    AND `the holder`'s `directs the manner in which the injured person works`

-- s 14(3): the principal must take reasonably practicable measures for "persons (other than a person referred to in subsection
-- (1)(a), (b) or (c) working under the principal's direction) who may be affected by any undertaking carried on by the
-- principal in the workplace".
GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder, `the person` IS AN Entrant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owes the section 14(3) duty to the person` IF
        `is the principal of the injured person's employer` `the holder`
    AND (NOT `owes the section 14(1) duty to the contractor's employee` `the holder` `the person`)
    AND `the holder`'s `carries on an undertaking in the workplace that may affect the injured person`

-- s 14A(1): the principal must take reasonably practicable measures to ensure that "any contractor engaged by the principal on or
-- after 1 September 2011 -- (a) has the necessary expertise to carry out the work ...; and (b) has taken adequate safety and
-- health measures in respect of any machinery, equipment, plant, article or process used, or to be used, by the contractor or
-- any employee employed by the contractor". (2), (3): including ascertaining training, licences, a risk assessment, and that
-- affected persons were informed. (6): "Section 14 does not limit the duty of a principal under this section" -- so s 14A does
-- not depend on the s 14(2) direction test.
GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `owes the section 14A duty about the contractor's expertise and measures` IF
        `is the principal of the injured person's employer` `the holder`
    AND `the holder`'s `date the contractor was engaged as yyyymmdd` AT LEAST 20110901

§§ `10 -- several capacities, the same duty on several persons`

-- s 10: "(a) a person may at any one time be 2 or more of the following: (i) an employer; ... (iv) a principal; ... (vi) an
-- occupier of a workplace ...; (b) this Act may at any one time impose the same duty or liability on 2 or more persons, whether in
-- the same capacity or in different capacities; and (c) a duty or liability imposed by this Act on any person is not diminished
-- or affected by the fact that it is imposed on one or more other persons".
-- So each duty-holder is tested on its own facts; nothing about the other party's duties enters the tests above. The rule is
-- stated as a function that ignores its argument.
GIVEN `another person owes a duty to the same person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty is diminished because another also owes one` IF
    FALSE

-- Count of the heads of Part 4 duty encoded here that one duty-holder owes on the facts (ss 11, 12(1), 12(2), 14(1), 14(3),
-- 14A, 19(2)(c)). A helper for comparing the two parties; the Act itself does not count.
GIVEN `b` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if` MEANS
    IF `b` THEN 1 ELSE 0

GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder, `the premises` IS A Premises, `the spot` IS A Spot, `the person` IS AN Entrant
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of duty heads owed` MEANS
        `one if` (`owes the section 11 occupier's duty to the person for the spot` `the holder` `the premises` `the spot` `the person`)
    PLUS `one if` (`owes the section 12(1) duty to the person as its employee` `the holder` `the person`)
    PLUS `one if` (`owes the section 12(2) duty to the person as a non-employee` `the holder`)
    PLUS `one if` (`owes the section 14(1) duty to the contractor's employee` `the holder` `the person`)
    PLUS `one if` (`owes the section 14(3) duty to the person` `the holder` `the person`)
    PLUS `one if` (`owes the section 14A duty about the contractor's expertise and measures` `the holder`)
    PLUS `one if` (`owes the section 19 common-area duty for access and egress` `the holder` `the spot`)

§§ `21(2) -- who may be served with an order`

-- s 21(2): "the Commissioner may serve a remedial order or a stop-work order in respect of a workplace on -- (a) any person who is
-- in control of the workplace, or the work or process carried out in the workplace; (b) any person whose duty under this Act is
-- to ensure the safety, health and welfare of any person at work in the workplace; or (c) any person who poses or is likely to
-- pose a risk to the safety, health and welfare of any person at work in the workplace." (Only where s 21(1) applies, which is
-- not modelled.)
GIVEN `the holder` IS A DutyHolder, `the premises` IS A Premises, `the spot` IS A Spot, `the person` IS AN Entrant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be served with a remedial or stop-work order` IF
        `the holder`'s `has charge, management or control of the workplace`
    OR  (    `the person`'s `is at work`
         AND `the number of duty heads owed` `the holder` `the premises` `the spot` `the person` GREATER THAN 0)
    OR  `the holder`'s `poses a risk to persons at work in the workplace`

§§ `59 -- other written law`

-- s 59: "Nothing in this Act or in any approved code of practice derogates from the effect of any other written law for the time
-- being in force." With s 60(1)(b) (in wsha-duties.l4), this is as near as the Act comes to the Work Injury Compensation Act: it
-- does not name it here, and does not say what that Act provides.
GIVEN `the other law` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act derogates from the other written law` IF
    FALSE
